File: record/devlog.d/2026/09/05/061947.md
---
---
title: 'The uncited principles, and the file the reference machinery could not see'
created: '2026-09-05T06:19:47'
tags: [record]
---

**Three principles had zero citations, and the three reasons turned out to be
different.** [DP-012](../../record/principles.d/DP-012.md) says a rule nothing points at is a rule nobody knows
applies to them, which reads as a prompt to go and add citations. That would
have been gaming the count. Asking *why* each was uncited was the useful move,
and only one of the three answers was "the principle is dead" — none of them,
in fact.

**[DP-008](../../record/principles.d/DP-008.md) was in force the whole time, in a file nothing scanned.**
`CONTRIBUTING.md` has a section headed *"Every change ships its record entry"*
whose first line is *"Run `luria new` in the same branch as the work"*. That is
[DP-008](../../record/principles.d/DP-008.md)'s claim restated verbatim, at the place contributors actually read
it, citing nothing. The same page states [DP-006](../../record/principles.d/DP-006.md) (*fire a new guard on a
real case before trusting it*), [DP-003](../../record/principles.d/DP-003.md) (*generated files are never edited
by hand*) and the [DP-001](../../record/principles.d/DP-001.md)/[DP-010](../../record/principles.d/DP-010.md) split between a failing check and a
report — five principles, zero citations.

The cause is that `doc_refs.doc_files()` listed `README.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and
`AGENTS.md` and stopped. That set was drawn as *the files an agent bootstraps
from*, which is a real category and the wrong one: what the reference rules
care about is prose that asserts the project's rules to a reader.
`CONTRIBUTING.md` is exactly that. So nothing linked its references, nothing
checked them, and the citation report counted a principle as uncited while the
page enforcing it sat one directory away.

**That is the second instance of the same gap, which is what made it worth
fixing rather than noting.** The first was `examples/README.md`, where a
hand-written `[ADR-077](../docs/decisions/ADR-077.md)` pointed at a path that
does not exist — an index-render scheme publishes its sources in place, so
`docs/decisions/` holds only the generated index. The site staging test caught
that one; nothing would have caught a bad reference in `CONTRIBUTING.md` at
all. Adding the file to the scanned set surfaced no violations, which is the
good outcome: the page was correct, and now it is *checked*.

**[DP-007](../../record/principles.d/DP-007.md) and [DP-011](../../record/principles.d/DP-011.md) are genuinely uncited, and correctly so.**
[DP-007](../../record/principles.d/DP-007.md) — no private brains — has its application in what `luria init`
writes into an agent file and in [#140](https://github.com/dmarx/luria/issues/140), assembling `CLAUDE.md` from
fragments. That is an open question, not a decided one, so there is no decision
for it to have shaped yet. [DP-011](../../record/principles.d/DP-011.md) — pick up the debt you encounter — is a
contributor's posture with no mechanism behind it anywhere in this repository.
By [DP-005](../../record/principles.d/DP-005.md) it sits at rung one, prose, and nothing has walked it up. Both
are honest zeros, and neither is improved by a citation manufactured to clear
it.

**And a decision's consequences age even when the decision holds.**
[ADR-045](../../record/decisions.d/ADR-045.md)'s consequences paragraph said `examples/**` joins `template/**` in
the site's exclusions. [ADR-077](../../record/decisions.d/ADR-077.md) reversed exactly that, and the other half of
the same paragraph — two `ADR`-scheme limits documented rather than resolved —
had already been overtaken by [ADR-047](../../record/decisions.d/ADR-047.md). The decision itself is untouched:
worked configurations are still executable examples. [ADR-017](../../record/decisions.d/ADR-017.md) had already
set the pattern for this, and it is the right one — *its body stands as
written, which is what a record is for, and this decision is where a reader
learns the state changed back.* So [ADR-077](../../record/decisions.d/ADR-077.md) carries the note and
[ADR-045](../../record/decisions.d/ADR-045.md) is not edited. Superseding it would have retired a decision that
is still in force to fix a sentence about its side effects.



